{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StructuralRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StructuralRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Lattice.Fold","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.DivisionRing","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.DFinsupp","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.SupIndep","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.DirectSum.Module"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.toRankDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.toRankDecomposition","kind":"def","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L343-L377","doc":"**Translation to ℕ-rank class.**\n\nGiven a `PanelImageStructure` over a finite-dimensional ambient\nspace, build a `PanelRankDecomposition` instance with\n`blockRank μ ν := finrank K (W μ ν)`,\n`jointRankMu μ := finrank K (W μ (νStar μ))`, and\n`totalRank := finrank K (⨆ μ ν, W μ ν)`.\n\nThe within-μ field follows from `finrank_iSup_eq_finset_sup`.\nThe across-μ field uses `finrank_iSup_eq_sum_of_iSupIndep` after\nrewriting the inner `⨆ ν` to its νStar value via\n`iSup_eq_νStar`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.finrank_iSup_eq_sum_of_iSupIndep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.finrank_iSup_eq_sum_of_iSupIndep","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L310-L339","doc":"**Finrank of an independent supremum decomposes as a sum.**\n\nFor an `iSupIndep` family of submodules in a finite-dimensional\nspace, the finrank of the joint supremum is the sum of the\nindividual finranks.\n\nProof: `DirectSum.coeLinearMap p : (⨁ i, p i) →ₗ[K] V` has\nrange `⨆ i, p i` (`DirectSum.range_coeLinearMap`), and is\ninjective by `iSupIndep.dfinsupp_lsum_injective`.  So\n`(⨁ i, p i) ≃ₗ[K] (⨆ i, p i)`, and the conclusion follows\nfrom `Module.finrank_directSum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.finrank_iSup_eq_finset_sup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.finrank_iSup_eq_finset_sup","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L284-L304","doc":"**Within-μ finrank equals the sup-over-ν of block finranks.**\n\nCombines the chain hypothesis (every block ≤ νStar-block) with\nfinrank monotonicity: the supremum's finrank equals the\nνStar-block's finrank, which is also the maximum of the\nindividual ν-block finranks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.finrank_blockRank_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.finrank_blockRank_le","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L269-L282","doc":"**finrank-monotonicity over the within-μ chain.**\n\nSince `W μ ν ≤ W μ (νStar μ)`, finrank is monotone on\nsub-spaces of a finite-dimensional space, so every block's\nfinrank is at most the `νStar`-block's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.finrank_iSup_eq_νStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.finrank_iSup_eq_νStar","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L254-L267","doc":"**Within-μ finrank equals the chain-maximum's finrank.**\n\nCombines `iSup_eq_νStar` with `finrank` (no monotonicity\nneeded since the supremum is literally the maximum element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.iSup_eq_νStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.iSup_eq_νStar","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L240-L252","doc":"**Within-μ joint span equals the maximum chain element.**\n\nFrom the chain hypothesis (`νStar_max`), every ν-block is\ncontained in the `νStar`-block, so `⨆ ν, W μ ν = W μ (νStar μ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.independent","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L235-L235","doc":"Across-μ independence of the per-μ joint sub-spaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.νStar_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.νStar_max","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L233-L233","doc":"Within-μ nesting: `νStar μ` dominates every ν in the inclusion order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.νStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.νStar","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L231-L231","doc":"A maximizing ν for each μ (witness of the chain's top element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L222-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelImageStructure","kind":"class","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L209-L236","doc":"**Panel-image Submodule structure.**\n\nA finite-dimensional ambient space `V` over a field `K`,\ntogether with a `(μ, ν)`-indexed family of sub-spaces\n`W : (μ : μIdx) → νIdx μ → Submodule K V` carrying the two\nstructural hypotheses of the audit:\n\n1. For each μ, there is a maximizing `νStar μ` such that\n   `W μ ν ≤ W μ (νStar μ)` for all ν (within-μ chain).\n2. The per-μ joint sub-spaces `W μ (νStar μ)` are\n   complete-lattice-independent (across-μ orthogonality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.panel_7_2_total_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.panel_7_2_total_rank","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L170-L177","doc":"**Empirical match** — the rank formula yields 86 at λ = [7, 2]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instPanelRankDecompositionBoolFinOfNatNatPanel_7_2_blockRankPanel_7_2_jointRankMu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instPanelRankDecompositionBoolFinOfNatNatPanel_7_2_blockRankPanel_7_2_jointRankMu","kind":"instance","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L163-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.panel_7_2_jointRankMu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.panel_7_2_jointRankMu","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L158-L161","doc":"The per-μ joint rank: `max_ν` of `panel_7_2_blockRank`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.panel_7_2_blockRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.panel_7_2_blockRank","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L147-L156","doc":"**λ = [7, 2] empirical rank decomposition** —\nencoded as a `PanelRankDecomposition` instance over the two\nLR-support μ-partitions and their respective ν-blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.rank_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.rank_formula","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L111-L127","doc":"**Structural rank formula** (derived).\n\nGiven the within-μ nesting and across-μ independence\nhypotheses, the total rank of the panel matrix is the sum\nover μ of the maximum over ν of the per-block rank.  Pure ℕ\narithmetic — proved unconditionally from the class fields. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.total_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.total_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L106-L106","doc":"**Across-μ independence** (Wedderburn block-diagonality for\n`H_n(q)` semisimple; standard).  Total rank decomposes\nadditively across μ-blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.joint_eq_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.joint_eq_max","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L100-L100","doc":"**Within-μ nesting** (Mackey/Specht filtration; cf. Mathas\n2004, Hu–Mathas 2012).  The joint column-span rank across\nall ν-blocks for a fixed μ equals the maximum of the\nindividual ν-block ranks — column spaces vary as a nested\nchain in ν, not as a direct sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PanelRankDecomposition","kind":"class","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StructuralRank.lean#L72-L107","doc":"**Structural rank decomposition class** for a Hecke panel\nmatrix indexed by `(μ, ν)`-blocks.\n\nClass hypotheses encode the two structural facts from the audit:\n(a) within-μ nesting (joint = max), and\n(b) across-μ independence (total = sum of joints).\n\nConjectural status: §3b-cond.  The within-μ nesting field is\nthe Mackey-filtration / Specht-filtration nesting (Mathas 2004;\nHu–Mathas 2012), specialized to test-panel column spaces.  Not\nexplicitly stated in the published literature for the\nfitting-matrix / column-rank shape used here, but mechanically\na corollary of those filtration results once the column spaces\nare identified with Specht-filtration layers. ","signatureChunk":0}]}